## Exercise 183

A valid display answer needs the actual pair of curves for each source equation and an intersection-based construction, not merely a generic instruction to draw or an algebraic solution.

ungraded genuinely required graph construction; do not pretend root-only checking verifies the requested method
- a) domain x != 0; curves y=6/x and y=x-1.
  Construction: Use common axes. Plot hyperbola points(-6,-1),(-3,-2),(-2,-3),(-1,-6),(1,6),(2,3),(3,2),(6,1); keep branches in quadrantsI andIII, with x=0,y=0 asymptotes. Draw line through(0,-1),(1,0). Read x-coordinates of both intersections.
  Intersections: (-2,-3); (3,2).
  Roots: -2; 3.
  Cross-check: x^2-x-6=(x-3)(x+2)=0; both roots obey x!=0.
- b) domain x != 0; curves y=6/x and y=x+3.
  Construction: Reuse hyperbola on common axes; draw line through(0,3),(-3,0). Locate one positive-x and one negative-x intersection. Read x approximately1.37 and-4.37. Exact roots are supplementary verification, not a replacement for graph construction.
  Intersections: ((-3-sqrt(33))/2,(3-sqrt(33))/2); ((-3+sqrt(33))/2,(3+sqrt(33))/2).
  Roots: \frac{-3-\sqrt{33}}{2}; \frac{-3+\sqrt{33}}{2}.
  Cross-check: x^2+3x-6=0 has discriminant33; product of roots-6, sum-3. Both roots nonzero.

